# GitHub Push Default

Always push to **https://github.com/haminxx** using GitHub username **haminxx**.

## Before push

If credential username is not set, run:

```bash
git config --global credential.https://github.com.username haminxx
```

Verify with:

```bash
git config --get credential.https://github.com.username
```

Expected remote for this project: `https://github.com/haminxx/Portfolio.git` (`git remote get-url origin`).

## Authentication

A PAT or token is still required via **Windows Credential Manager**. Setting the GitHub credential username avoids account-picker confusion when multiple GitHub accounts are configured; it does not replace the token.

## Do not

- Store passwords or tokens in repository files
- Change `user.name` or `user.email` unless explicitly requested
